{"title":"Career roadmap — Eco-tourism Guide","role":"Eco-tourism Guide","summary":"An Eco-tourism Guide leads visitors through natural areas while explaining ecology, biodiversity, wildlife, local communities and conservation. The role combines environmental knowledge + tourism + interpretation + visitor safety + conservation awareness.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Environmental Studies / Ecology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build ecology, biodiversity, interpretation, field skills and tourism fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Work as an eco-tourism/nature guide in wildlife reserves, national parks, nature resorts or conservation organisations"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress into senior guiding, destination interpretation, eco-tourism programme management and conservation tourism"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Lead eco-tourism programmes, conservation-tourism initiatives, nature interpretation centres or sustainable tourism enterprises"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Environmental foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ecology"},{"text":"Biodiversity"},{"text":"Environmental science"},{"text":"Botany and zoology fundamentals"},{"text":"Ecosystems"},{"text":"Food chains and ecological interactions"},{"text":"Conservation biology"},{"text":"Climate change"},{"text":"Environmental pollution"},{"text":"Indian biodiversity"},{"text":"Protected areas"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Observation skills"},{"text":"Nature identification"},{"text":"Field-note writing"},{"text":"Public speaking"},{"text":"Basic photography"},{"text":"First-aid awareness"},{"text":"Outdoor safety"}]},{"type":"h","tex